# ── Documents of record. The formatter must never rewrite these. ──────────────
#
# tasks/      Plans are decision history (and gitignored). `prettier --write .`
#             reached in here and rewrote a plan's RESEARCH.md; a plan is never
#             ours to reformat.
# docs/       docs/spec.md is the signed-off authority that outranks CLAUDE.md and
#             is cited by section number throughout the codebase. Reflowing its
#             tables churns 197 lines of a document nobody agreed to change.
# CLAUDE.md   The rulebook. project-init T-10's "Done when" requires
#             `git diff CLAUDE.md` to show changes confined to ONE section, which a
#             whole-file reformat makes impossible to satisfy.
# .claude/    Skill definitions, not project source.
tasks/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

